.TH "TDISK-DELETE-PARTITION" "8" "2026-4-18" "TigerOS 0.2.1" "System Administration"

.SH NAME
tdisk-delete-partition \- delete a disk partition entry.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tdisk delete-partition
.I partition-num
[-q | --quiet]

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBdelete-partition\fR command deletes a disk partition entry.

.SH OPTIONS

partition-num
.RS 4
The partition number to delete. Use \fBtdisk list-partitions\fR to see the partition numbers.
.RE

-q, --quiet
.RS 4
Do not show the confirmation message to delete the partition.
.RE

-s, --shift
.RS 4
Shift the partition table to fill the deleted entry.
.RE

.SH AUTHOR

\fBtdisk\fR was created by tigercodes-dev \fB<https://github.com/tigercodes-dev>\fR as part of the TigerOS project.

